    "/internal/tenants/{tenant_id}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Tenant config + scope for peers (data scoping).\n\nA DELETED tenant answers 200 with `status: \"deleted\"` and `deleted_at` \u2014 it does NOT 404.\n\nThat is the whole point of the tombstone. `tenant.deleted` is published at most once, so a peer\nthat was restarting when it fired never heard it. If this 404'd, that peer would fail OPEN (an\nunknown tenant is usually an onboarding gap, not a punishment) and keep accepting writes to a\ncompany that no longer exists \u2014 for ever, because nothing would ever tell it again. Answering\nwith the tombstone makes the deletion something a peer LEARNS BY LOOKING. A read is\nself-healing; a missed event is wrong for ever.\n\nPeers: treat `status == \"deleted\"` as a hard stop. It is not an onboarding gap.\n\n`branding` is included so a render path (a PDF carrying the customer's logo) can read it with\nthe internal token alone, instead of minting a token with a cross-tenant admin capability just\nto fetch a logo. Least privilege: the smaller capability must be enough for the smaller job.",
        "operationId": "internal_get_internal_tenants__tenant_id__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "tenant_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Tenant Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "header",
            "name": "X-Internal-Token",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "title": "X-Internal-Token"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "additionalProperties": true,
                  "title": "Response Internal Get Internal Tenants  Tenant Id  Get",
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Internal Get",
        "tags": [
          "internal"
        ]
      }
    },
